but you just said,
"More firing than hiring."

00:51:46.542 --> 00:51:47.500
- [Gary] Yes.

00:51:47.500 --> 00:51:49.208
- [Woman] But you
can't just fire somebody

00:51:49.208 --> 00:51:52.208
like that, but what do
you do with your people

00:51:52.208 --> 00:51:55.041
to keep them motivated, keep
them going, keep them happy?

00:51:55.041 --> 00:51:56.041
- You got it.
- How do you do it?

00:51:56.041 --> 00:51:56.959
- [Gary] Great question.

00:51:56.959 --> 00:52:00.542
The thing we do that has
worked unbelievably well is

00:52:00.542 --> 00:52:03.333
I massively
over-invest in realizing

00:52:03.333 --> 00:52:05.250
that managing
people is the same way

00:52:05.250 --> 00:52:07.250
that I think about marketing.

00:52:07.250 --> 00:52:11.041
You can't have one 30 second
video that works for everybody.

00:52:11.041 --> 00:52:14.083
I have no idea what
those three care about.

00:52:14.083 --> 00:52:15.875
Somebody might care about money.

00:52:15.875 --> 00:52:17.959
Somebody might care
about work-life balance.

00:52:17.959 --> 00:52:20.208
Somebody might
care about notoriety.

00:52:20.208 --> 00:52:22.917
Some might care about
football as their passion,

00:52:22.917 --> 00:52:24.458
and I get them
tickets to the World Cup.

00:52:24.458 --> 00:52:28.834
I don't care what my
800 employees want in life,

00:52:28.834 --> 00:52:31.500
I just want to know what it is.

00:52:31.500 --> 00:52:33.708
- [Woman] When you
started, in the beginning,

00:52:33.708 --> 00:52:37.291
were you surrounded
by young people or...?

00:52:37.291 --> 00:52:38.250
- Both.

00:52:38.250 --> 00:52:39.875
When I started the wine
business, I was surrounded

00:52:39.875 --> 00:52:43.542
by older people, and I was
22, and that was challenging

00:52:43.542 --> 00:52:45.125
'cause I had to break through.

00:52:45.125 --> 00:52:48.125
When I started Vayner,
I started it with young people,

00:52:48.125 --> 00:52:50.792
but it doesn't
matter how old or young.

00:52:50.792 --> 00:52:53.417
I hate when people are like,
"Millennials love work life."

00:52:53.417 --> 00:52:56.000
I know tons of
millennials that just want cash.

00:52:56.000 --> 00:52:57.834
You know, like,
everybody's different.

00:52:57.834 --> 00:52:59.333
When I started out it was easy.

00:52:59.333 --> 00:53:01.959
There was only six people
to know every single thing

00:53:01.959 --> 00:53:03.291
that they cared
about in the world.

00:53:03.291 --> 00:53:04.333
Now it's hard.

00:53:04.333 --> 00:53:06.000
Now I've built a
lot of infrastructure.

00:53:06.000 --> 00:53:08.250
Now I run a lot of big
data to see what their posting

00:53:08.250 --> 00:53:11.125
in social media to know what
they care about in their lives.

00:53:11.125 --> 00:53:15.125
I'm obsessed with
knowing what my 800 people want,

00:53:15.125 --> 00:53:16.875
because then I can
reverse engineer it,

00:53:16.875 --> 00:53:18.875
because I work for them.

00:53:21.208 --> 00:53:23.792
Leadership is understanding
that people don't work for you.

00:53:23.792 --> 00:53:26.333
Leadership is understanding
that you work for them,

00:53:26.333 --> 00:53:29.000
and the best way to build a
great company is retention,

00:53:29.000 --> 00:53:30.500
keeping people forever.

00:53:30.500 --> 00:53:33.041
My mission, my obsession,
is that everybody that walks

00:53:33.041 --> 00:53:34.542
through VaynerMedia
works for me

00:53:34.542 --> 00:53:36.500
for the rest of their lives.

00:53:36.500 --> 00:53:38.333
To be able to do that,
I need to know what they care

00:53:38.333 --> 00:53:41.583
about at 24, what
they care about at 29,

00:53:41.583 --> 00:53:42.625
what they care about at 35.

00:53:42.625 --> 00:53:43.834
Oh wait, they fell in love.

00:53:43.834 --> 00:53:47.542
Oh wait, their
husband wants to move to L.A.

00:53:47.542 --> 00:53:50.708
I have to be flexible, nimble,
I have to pay attention,

00:53:50.708 --> 00:53:52.542
I have to be obsessed.

00:53:53.625 --> 00:53:55.000
- [Woman] I'm starting today.

00:53:55.000 --> 00:53:56.333
I'm going to be obsessed.
- Love it.

00:53:56.333 --> 00:53:57.291
- [Woman] Okay.

00:53:57.291 --> 00:53:58.166
- How many people?

00:53:58.166 --> 00:53:59.166
Hold on to it, this is fun.

00:53:59.166 --> 00:54:01.041
How many people do you have?

00:54:01.041 --> 00:54:03.125
- [Woman] My boss has a lot
of people working for him.

00:54:03.125 --> 00:54:04.208
- Yep.
(audience laughter)

00:54:04.208 --> 00:54:05.333
- Around 150--
- So you and your boss

00:54:05.333 --> 00:54:08.375
and for him, I'm telling
you this is an amazing way

00:54:08.375 --> 00:54:10.125
to build a great company.

00:54:10.125 --> 00:54:12.291
You have to take
15 and 20 minutes,

00:54:12.291 --> 00:54:13.458
you have to take a dinner.

00:54:13.458 --> 00:54:15.291
If somebody's very
important, it's dinner

00:54:15.291 --> 00:54:16.834
once a quarter, twice a year.

00:54:16.834 --> 00:54:18.083
If it's somebody new--
- [Woman] Alright!

00:54:18.083 --> 00:54:19.708
- What's that?
(audience laughter)

00:54:19.708 --> 00:54:20.542
Got it!

00:54:20.542 --> 00:54:21.917
- [Woman] You can
come with us! (laughs)

00:54:21.917 --> 00:54:22.875
- But you know what I mean?

00:54:22.875 --> 00:54:23.834
That's the key.

00:54:23.834 --> 00:54:25.291
I mean some of you
that watch my vlog,

00:54:25.291 --> 00:54:27.625
you see five minute meetings
with every single person

00:54:27.625 --> 00:54:28.625
that comes in.

00:54:28.625 --> 00:54:31.417
It's five minutes, you
can't accomplish that much,

00:54:31.417 --> 00:54:33.959
but let me tell you why I do it.

00:54:33.959 --> 00:54:34.917
Some people try to razz me,

00:54:34.917 --> 00:54:36.291
they think I'm
doing it for show.

00:54:36.291 --> 00:54:37.625
I'm not doing it for show.

00:54:37.625 --> 00:54:39.041
By sitting with
you for five minutes,

00:54:39.041 --> 00:54:40.375
knowing your name, 
knowing your phone,

00:54:40.375 --> 00:54:42.375
I remember a lot of stuff too.

00:54:42.375 --> 00:54:45.041
Knowing if you have a brother
or sister, or you like sports.

00:54:45.041 --> 00:54:47.834
When I go into
the elevator with you

00:54:47.834 --> 00:54:50.208
in three months
and we go up together

00:54:50.208 --> 00:54:52.708
and we can have a 3 minute
conversation, I'm chipping away.

00:54:52.708 --> 00:54:54.125
They're scared to talk to me.

00:54:54.125 --> 00:54:56.583
I'm the CEO, and
not only am I the CEO,

00:54:56.583 --> 00:54:59.583
I'm also internet
famous and a CEO.

00:54:59.583 --> 00:55:01.959
So it's really hard for
them to get comfortable,

00:55:01.959 --> 00:55:04.125
and I need them to
feel safe to tell me

00:55:04.125 --> 00:55:06.708
when something's wrong.

00:55:06.708 --> 00:55:08.959
That's the key because the cost

00:55:08.959 --> 00:55:13.166
of somebody leaving
is so great, so great.

00:55:13.166 --> 00:55:16.875
Much more expensive
than the 15 to 19 hours

00:55:16.875 --> 00:55:19.625
that you deploy to stay close,

00:55:19.625 --> 00:55:22.500
and remembering that you
need to give them more value

00:55:22.500 --> 00:55:23.583
than they're giving to you.

00:55:23.583 --> 00:55:27.375
I hate when
leaders, founders, bosses,

00:55:27.375 --> 00:55:30.083
expect people to
work as hard as they do.

00:55:30.083 --> 00:55:31.917
If you want them to
work as hard as you do,

00:55:31.917 --> 00:55:34.291
give them the same economics.

00:55:36.542 --> 00:55:38.125
My friend's always like,
"Gary, I can't get my people

00:55:38.125 --> 00:55:39.625
"to work as hard as me."

00:55:39.625 --> 00:55:41.458
I'm like, "How much do
they own of the company?"

00:55:41.458 --> 00:55:42.291
"Nothing."

00:55:42.291 --> 00:55:44.375
I'm like, "That's
a starting point."

00:55:44.375 --> 00:55:46.333
(audience laughter)

00:55:46.333 --> 00:55:48.792
I don't expect
anybody to work as hard as me.

00:55:48.792 --> 00:55:50.583
They need to
care about themselves.

00:55:50.583 --> 00:55:53.041
They need to execute
for what they're doing.

00:55:53.041 --> 00:55:56.583
And then, people are motivated
by very different things.

00:55:56.583 --> 00:55:57.542
It's been so interesting to me,

00:55:57.542 --> 00:55:59.500
I'm using soccer,
slash your football,

00:55:59.500 --> 00:56:01.667
because it's such a
passion in this country.

00:56:01.667 --> 00:56:03.917
There's a kid that works
for me, who flat-out told me

00:56:03.917 --> 00:56:05.208
that he was considering to leave

00:56:05.208 --> 00:56:06.375
because he got offered double--

00:56:06.375 --> 00:56:07.708
You know,
Vayner's in tough spot.

00:56:07.708 --> 00:56:10.041
We're so hot,
and we're so young,

00:56:10.041 --> 00:56:12.083
and there's such big
advertisers in the world

00:56:12.083 --> 00:56:13.458
that are trying
to steal our people.

00:56:13.458 --> 00:56:16.000
He's like, "Somebody
offered me double my salary.

00:56:16.000 --> 00:56:17.500
"But three weeks earlier,

00:56:17.500 --> 00:56:20.458
"because you knew I was
a St. Louis baseball fan,

00:56:20.458 --> 00:56:21.834
"you came to me and
I was doing a good job,

00:56:21.834 --> 00:56:22.750
"and you gave me two tickets."

00:56:22.750 --> 00:56:23.708
Randomly.

00:56:23.708 --> 00:56:27.625
Not his anniversary,
not his birthday, randomly.

00:56:27.625 --> 00:56:29.000
He's like, "That made me stay."

00:56:29.000 --> 00:56:30.208
And now he's one of
the most important people

00:56:30.208 --> 00:56:32.458
in our paid media team.

00:56:32.458 --> 00:56:34.708
Those tickets cost me $937.

00:56:38.250 --> 00:56:39.667
- [Woman] Okay, 
thank you. (laughs)

00:56:39.667 --> 00:56:41.250
(audience laughter)
- [Gary] What's that?

00:56:41.250 --> 00:56:43.500
- [Woman] He gave us Gary.

00:56:43.500 --> 00:56:45.166
- There you go.

00:56:45.166 --> 00:56:48.250
It's amazing, but for
other people, I try to do it,

00:56:48.250 --> 00:56:50.583
and they're like take your
fucking trip to Florida back.

00:56:50.583 --> 00:56:52.417
Give me $3000, asshole.

00:56:52.417 --> 00:56:54.667
You know, like, you
have to know the person.

00:56:54.667 --> 00:56:57.083
Everybody has
their own North Star.

00:56:57.083 --> 00:57:01.375
- [Woman] Okay.
- Thank you.

00:57:01.375 --> 00:57:02.291
Two more?

00:57:04.041 --> 00:57:05.208
You know, I love this.

00:57:05.208 --> 00:57:06.667
- [William] Hi Gary.
- Hey.

00:57:06.667 --> 00:57:07.500
- [William] My name is William,

00:57:07.500 --> 00:57:09.708
I've been working for
a year now at a startup.

00:57:09.708 --> 00:57:12.166
We've gone from three to
fifteen employees...

