close to as many people.

00:57:38.083 --> 00:57:40.959
I would go into Instagram,
and Facebook fan pages,

00:57:40.959 --> 00:57:43.041
and I would
message them, by hand.

00:57:43.041 --> 00:57:45.583
- [William] Alright. Do
you have a Facebook account?

00:57:45.583 --> 00:57:47.708
- I do, slash Gary.

00:57:49.708 --> 00:57:53.500
But remember,
when you approach slash Gary,

00:57:53.500 --> 00:57:56.000
figure out what Gary cares
about, not what you care about.

00:57:56.000 --> 00:57:58.000
- [William] Alright, 
the market's always right. 

00:57:58.000 --> 00:57:59.875
Thank you.
- You got it. 

00:57:59.875 --> 00:58:01.542
Yeah, the
market is always right, man.

00:58:01.542 --> 00:58:03.333
I'm really glad you
ended with that, bro,

00:58:03.333 --> 00:58:05.417
because if you
actually internalize that, 

00:58:05.417 --> 00:58:07.667
so much changes.

00:58:07.667 --> 00:58:11.333
Too much ego in the world,
people think they are so smart,

00:58:11.333 --> 00:58:13.917
they latch onto
things like, they latch onto

00:58:13.917 --> 00:58:15.208
the guy who created the Porsche,

00:58:15.208 --> 00:58:17.166
or the guy that
created the automobile,

00:58:17.166 --> 00:58:20.750
legendary, all time billionaire
visionaries, and they go

00:58:20.750 --> 00:58:24.458
"Yeah okay, but if Henry Ford
listened to his customers,

00:58:24.458 --> 00:58:26.542
