they don't work together.

01:01:37.417 --> 01:01:38.625
- [Sophie] No they don't.
- Never.

01:01:38.625 --> 01:01:41.458
That's not, you know, some
things are great in theory.

01:01:41.458 --> 01:01:43.375
It's great on paper, let's get

01:01:43.375 --> 01:01:45.000
an above the line
traditional agency,

01:01:45.000 --> 01:01:46.375
a digital agency,
a social agency,

01:01:46.375 --> 01:01:48.625
and they'll all work together.
Great on paper.

01:01:48.625 --> 01:01:51.166
You know what else is
great on paper? Communism.

01:01:51.166 --> 01:01:52.625
(audience laughter)

01:01:52.625 --> 01:01:56.375
It's great. Like if you read it,
it seems really good,

01:01:56.375 --> 01:01:59.333
it just doesn't
match to the human spirit.

01:01:59.333 --> 01:02:01.458
You can't ask two
companies who both want

01:02:01.458 --> 01:02:03.208
to build their
business to play nice,

01:02:03.208 --> 01:02:04.583
when they're both
undermining each other

01:02:04.583 --> 01:02:06.667
to get more business.

01:02:06.667 --> 01:02:08.000
And that's why my
companies really worked

01:02:08.000 --> 01:02:11.041
in the sandbox, because
I've taught all my people

01:02:11.041 --> 01:02:13.417
to just assume that's
what everybody's doing.

01:02:13.417 --> 01:02:15.375
We're not mad when the
agencies do that to us,

01:02:15.375 --> 01:02:17.250
that's what
they're supposed to do.

01:02:17.250 --> 01:02:19.000
What I tell them
to do, my people,

01:02:19.000 --> 01:02:23.125
even the most senior, is to
eat shit, be the bigger person.

01:02:23.125 --> 01:02:26.458
I'll take care of it up here,
and it's worked very well

01:02:26.458 --> 01:02:29.875
cause the client can feel who
is trying to make it work,

01:02:29.875 --> 01:02:31.750
and who's not.

01:02:31.750 --> 01:02:33.708
- [Sophie] Alright, thank you.
- Cool, yep.

01:02:33.708 --> 01:02:35.208
- A couple more
and then we'll go.

01:02:35.208 --> 01:02:36.041
- [Yama] Hello.
- Hello.

01:02:36.041 --> 01:02:37.792
