I thank my entire family

01:03:05.041 --> 01:03:07.333
and one random person:

01:03:07.333 --> 01:03:10.959
Travis, the founder
and CEO of Uber.

01:03:10.959 --> 01:03:13.750
Travis came to me, and
wanted me to invest in Uber,

01:03:13.750 --> 01:03:17.792
and I passed, twice.

01:03:17.792 --> 01:03:19.041
That $50,000 investment,

01:03:19.041 --> 01:03:21.333
because that was the
size of what I was writing,

01:03:21.333 --> 01:03:25.125
would now be worth
close to $400 million.

01:03:25.125 --> 01:03:26.542
That's a bad move.

01:03:26.542 --> 01:03:28.750
(audience laughter)

01:03:31.125 --> 01:03:33.875
So that's, that's not
as valuable to everybody.

01:03:33.875 --> 01:03:35.792
I'll tell you what's
valuable to everybody.

01:03:35.792 --> 01:03:40.333
Every time in my
career that my eyes got big,

01:03:40.333 --> 01:03:41.750
and I decided,

01:03:41.750 --> 01:03:43.333
so what I do very
well, I referenced

01:03:43.333 --> 01:03:45.417
the 100 and 67 million thing,

01:03:45.417 --> 01:03:48.792
I'm very good at making
80% of my business stable,

01:03:48.792 --> 01:03:52.041
tried-and-true,
staying the course,

01:03:52.041 --> 01:03:54.083
continuing to do
what I know will work,

01:03:54.083 --> 01:03:56.750
and then taking 20%
of my money and energy

01:03:56.750 --> 01:03:59.708
and being very risky,
and trying to put myself

01:03:59.708 --> 01:04:00.667
out of business.

01:04:00.667 --> 01:04:02.667
Back to the agency
question, what's the agency

01:04:02.667 --> 01:04:04.750
that's coming next
that could hurt me.

01:04:04.750 --> 01:04:07.625
Is it a VR shop? I'm trying
to put myself out of business.

01:04:07.625 --> 01:04:09.250
I'm very good at that,
and that's why I build

01:04:09.250 --> 01:04:11.959
very big businesses. I'm not
as profitable every year,

01:04:11.959 --> 01:04:14.667
but I get really big, got it?

01:04:14.667 --> 01:04:17.959
When I've taken
that out of my control,

01:04:17.959 --> 01:04:21.792
and have given
money and some energy

01:04:21.792 --> 01:04:25.667
to other companies and put
a founder and CEO in charge,

01:04:25.667 --> 01:04:28.083
like I did after
I left Wine Library

01:04:28.083 --> 01:04:30.917
and started VaynerMedia for a
social network called Cork'd,

01:04:30.917 --> 01:04:32.875
which was a wine social network,

01:04:32.875 --> 01:04:35.750
for a company called
Forrest, which was a designer

01:04:35.750 --> 01:04:39.875
and developer social network,
where I was the "co-founder",

01:04:39.875 --> 01:04:41.708
but I really wasn't
running the company,

01:04:41.708 --> 01:04:43.291
it was mainly,
I was giving money,

01:04:43.291 --> 01:04:46.792
we leveraged my name, I would
check in once in a while,

01:04:46.792 --> 01:04:49.375
I've done very poorly.

01:04:49.375 --> 01:04:54.208
- So, what I've
learned is, when I'm operating

01:04:54.208 --> 01:04:56.917
and building scale around me,
it's a very good strategy,

01:04:56.917 --> 01:05:00.208
financially worthwhile,
when I've gotten big eyes

01:05:00.208 --> 01:05:02.417
and I wanna do
everything and support other

01:05:02.417 --> 01:05:05.834
entrepreneurs, in a
world where I try my best

01:05:05.834 --> 01:05:07.792
to vet them, but they
may be good or they may not

01:05:07.792 --> 01:05:11.667
be good, those have
been some of the places

01:05:11.667 --> 01:05:13.417
where I've made a mistake.

01:05:13.417 --> 01:05:15.166
And I think, I'll
be honest with you,

01:05:15.166 --> 01:05:19.333
I think my greatest
mistake is still ahead of me.

01:05:19.333 --> 01:05:21.166
Because of the way I play.

01:05:21.166 --> 01:05:26.000
Where I will have a
great mistake is that I hedged

01:05:26.000 --> 01:05:30.792
so much, I invest so much,
I'm building so much

01:05:30.792 --> 01:05:33.917
for the future,
that I may not achieve

01:05:33.917 --> 01:05:37.458
my great ambitions
because I left too many dollars

01:05:37.458 --> 01:05:39.375
along the way in
a thirty year macro

01:05:39.375 --> 01:05:44.208
and at 70 or 75 or 80, when
I realize shit, I don't have

01:05:44.208 --> 01:05:47.333
a lot more time, it
could get me into a place

01:05:47.333 --> 01:05:51.166
where I become
cynical and bitter

01:05:51.166 --> 01:05:52.417
because I left so much,

01:05:52.417 --> 01:05:53.959
I did so much
for everybody else.

01:05:53.959 --> 01:05:57.250
The 51-49 that I give to
everybody else hurt me

01:05:57.250 --> 01:06:01.041
in the end and so I could
become this weird character

01:06:01.041 --> 01:06:03.625
that goes and lives
in a cave out of anger

01:06:03.625 --> 01:06:05.625
in my old years and
young entrepreneurs are gonna

01:06:05.625 --> 01:06:08.250
try and find me
and shit like that so,

01:06:08.250 --> 01:06:10.708
that's how I think
my story could end.

01:06:10.708 --> 01:06:11.583
And I mean that.

01:06:11.583 --> 01:06:14.792
I think my greatest
failure is at the end.

01:06:14.792 --> 01:06:17.834
My intuition is I'll
convince myself that the journey

01:06:17.834 --> 01:06:20.708
and the legacy trumped
whatever materialistic thing

01:06:20.708 --> 01:06:24.750
I wanted, I kind of
already know that too, yeah.

01:06:25.708 --> 01:06:28.291
Okay, one more and then we
should get on schedule right,

01:06:28.291 --> 01:06:30.250
cause I'm fucking it up, yeah.

